      "content": "Yes, the risk is significant because dextromethorphan blocks serotonin reuptake like sertraline can, potentially triggering serotonin syndrome even at standard doses. For a productive cough, cough suppressants like dextromethorphan are generally not recommended as they can make mucus difficult to clear. You should ask your pharmacist or doctor about non-opioid alternatives like various honey-based syrups, guaifenesin (expectorants) if appropriate, or specific cough syrup formulations that explicitly exclude dextromethorphan. Do not increase any doses on your own, and please consult your healthcare provider for a prescription that won't compromise your depression treatment.",
